  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Transnational Cooperation and Fostering Peace: Natural and Mixed World Heritage in Asia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the spirit of UNESCO&#x2019;s peace-building mission, and particularly of culture as a vector for peace, resilience and sustainable development, the project aims to enhance transnational and regional cooperation to identify and conserve outstanding natural and mixed heritage in Asia by (1) addressing existing challenges for transnational conservation and improving the management of existing transnational World Heritage properties (state of conservation); and (2) identifying and mapping existing knowledge and capacity gaps, along with priorities for potential natural and mixed transboundary / serial transnational sites in Asia that could be considered for inscription on the World Heritage List, using technical and scientific criteria (nomination). The project will also aim to mainstream transnational conservation through awareness-raising and capacity-building activities at national and site levels.</narrative>
  </description>
